/*
 * Phase 06: the port's stylesheet.
 *
 * recompui loads this by name from <executable>/assets/recomp.rcss. Every
 * N64: Recompiled port has one, and it is deliberately almost empty.
 *
 * The menus are the same across these ports because the look is not in here.
 * recompui carries the theme in code, as a palette of named colours --
 * Background1..3, Text, Primary, Secondary, Warning, Danger, Success, Border --
 * with the defaults the other recomps use, and its elements style themselves
 * from it. A port that writes its own colours here does not restyle those
 * elements; it competes with them, and the result is a menu that is neither
 * one thing nor the other. So this file supplies the one thing the library
 * genuinely cannot know, which is the font, and otherwise stays out of the way.
 *
 * The family name is the one declared inside the .ttf, not its filename:
 * LatoLatin-Regular.ttf calls itself "LatoLatin". It must match what
 * src/frontend.cpp registers with register_primary_font. Getting it wrong fails
 * silently and strangely -- every element lays out and draws in the right
 * place, with no text in any of them.
 *
 * To restyle the menus, set theme colours from C++ with
 * recompui::theme::set_theme_color rather than adding rules here.
 */

body {
    font-family: LatoLatin;
    font-weight: normal;
    font-style: normal;
    font-size: 20dp;
}
